nread -- a terminal text reader
==============================

nread is a read-only fork of GNU nano. It keeps file browsing, search,
syntax highlighting, line numbers, soft wrapping, and multiple open files.
Typing and pasting cannot change the displayed text. There are no save,
replace, cut, undo, formatting, spell-checking, or command-execution controls.
Files are opened without editor lock files, and exiting never asks to save.

Usage
-----

    nread file.txt
    nread -l -S file.txt another.txt
    nread +42 file.txt
    command | nread -

Use arrow keys and Page Up/Down to navigate. Ctrl+F searches, Alt+W finds
another match, Ctrl+R opens another file, and Alt+, / Alt+. switch files.
Ctrl+X closes the current file and exits when no files remain. Ctrl+G shows
all shortcuts. Text selection and copying remain available for reading.
Use --help to see display and navigation options.

Configuration
-------------

nread retains nano's nanorc syntax. It looks for nreadrc in the configured
system location (normally /usr/local/etc), then /etc. If neither exists,
it looks for nanorc in those same locations. This lets a local build reuse
the system's installed /etc/nanorc without extra configure flags.
It then reads the first user configuration found in this order:

    ~/.nreadrc
    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nread/nreadrc
    ~/.config/nread/nreadrc
    ~/.nanorc
    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nano/nanorc
    ~/.config/nano/nanorc

Use -I to ignore configuration or -f FILE to read only a specific file.
Display settings, syntax definitions, and reader key bindings are supported.
Settings and bindings for disabled features are silently ignored; ignored
bindings leave existing reader shortcuts intact. Unknown settings still
report errors. Search and cursor-position history can be saved when
explicitly enabled with -H and -P or their configuration settings.

Build
-----

From this Git checkout:

    ./autogen.sh
    ./configure
    make
    ./src/nread README

The bootstrap requires Git, autoconf, automake, autopoint/gettext, and
downloads the pinned gnulib dependency. Building requires a C compiler,
make, pkg-config, and ncurses development headers. See README.hacking for
the inherited build prerequisites. Use ./configure --prefix=PATH to set
the installation location, then make install to install nread.

Run the reader regression checks after building (requires Python 3 and pyte):

    python3 tests/reader.py ./src/nread

